  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- Reviewer names this as a personal highlight of the show [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **130804 01**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **130804 01**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **130804 01**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **130804 01**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **130804 01**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **130804 01**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **130804 01**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **130804 01**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **MyMorningJacket2013-08-04** (recommended): source not stated; 11 songs; 74 min; rated 5/5 by 4 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer notes the recording flutters between channels because the microphones were moving with the music [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Show featured guests including Bob Weir and Ryan Bingham, among others, at Shoreline in Mountain View, California [1]\n- Reviewer mentions the set included guest sit-ins [3]\n- Reviewer sat in the tenth row, center, and was seeing the band for the first time [5]\n- Bob Weir joined the band on stage during the show [5]\n- Reviewer points to a separate recording of Wilco's set from the same date [2]\n- Reviewer was heading to see the band in Santa Barbara the next day [5]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **MyMorningJacket2013-08-04**: Recorded by Chris Berry from section 101 using a Sony PCM-M10 recorder and Church Audio CA11 cardioid mics, no preamp; Mics were placed at six feet with windscreens; captured at 48kHz/24-bit WAV, converted to FLAC in Goldwave, uploaded to archive [1]",
